# Credit-card rules for creditcard.csv — correct for ITS OWN data, and a clear
# mismatch for checking.csv.
#
# A deliberately different shape from checking.csv.rules, so the two reject each
# other for two DIFFERENT stage-1 reasons and neither rejection can be passing by
# accident:
#
#   this file vs checking.csv     — five fields, four columns: it addresses a
#                                   column the data does not have
#   checking.csv.rules vs this    — %m/%d/%Y cannot read 2024-02-03
#
# `category` is not an hledger field. hledger keeps it as a named CSV field so
# `%category` can be matched on, which is what the if-rules below do.

skip 1
fields date, code, description, amount, category
date-format %Y-%m-%d
currency $

account1 liabilities:creditcard:visa
account2 expenses:unknown

if %category Fees
    account2 expenses:banking:fees

if %category Groceries
    account2 expenses:food:groceries

if %category Payment
    account2 assets:bank:checking

if %category Dining
    account2 expenses:food:coffee
